From 6a5c5f520be666fd71e6b51d735875e10e782fc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:10:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: give threads their ring at start, and the process
 start time

Every node thread calls util::ThreadRename first; it now also gives the
thread its metrics ring, from the pool rings of exited threads return
to. A thread's first sample then neither locks nor allocates, and
short-lived threads (outbound dials) reuse rings instead of allocating.
Threads started before metrics (the scheduler) still get theirs on
their first sample.

Also exports the process start time (Prometheus convention: uptime is
time() - lotus_process_start_time_seconds), and adds benchmarks of a
disabled recording site and of rendering the node's whole registry.

(cherry picked from commit b908cc71ae4405ab1a7a7dc396c443154bf5e898)

N3-Source-Commit: b908cc71ae4405ab1a7a7dc396c443154bf5e898
N3-Source-Export: 0013
---
